    {
      "text": "%md\n\nTASK: Count the rows in the dataset.\n\nHIVE: `36 seconds`\nBASH: `17 seconds`\n\n\nThe delta is of a whopping `20 seconds`.\n\nThis is primarily due to their architectural design. \n\nBash operates directly on the filesystem with minimal overhead, making it quick for small and local tasks.\n\nHive, on the other hand goes through multiple layers to process the data. It involves parsing SQL, accessing metadata from metastore, applying schema checks and later triggering a MR | Tez job.\n\nWhile Hive was slow for this task, it is optimal for a larger and complex data job.",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2025-07-23T21:44:22+0000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "tableHide": false,
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "colWidth": 12,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "fontSize": 9,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "results": {
        "code": "SUCCESS",
        "msg": [
          {
            "type": "HTML",
            "data": "<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<p>TASK: Count the rows in the dataset.</p>\n<p>HIVE: <code>36 seconds</code><br />\nBASH: <code>17 seconds</code></p>\n<p>The delta is of a whopping <code>20 seconds</code>.</p>\n<p>This is primarily due to their architectural design.</p>\n<p>Bash operates directly on the filesystem with minimal overhead, making it quick for small and local tasks.</p>\n<p>Hive, on the other hand goes through multiple layers to process the data. It involves parsing SQL, accessing metadata from metastore, applying schema checks and later triggering a MR | Tez job.</p>\n<p>While Hive was slow for this task, it is optimal for a larger and complex data job.</p>\n\n</div>"
          }
        ]
      },
